<title>SOUTH KOREA: Korea Heavy Ind in China ship engine joint venture.</title>
<headline>Korea Heavy Ind in China ship engine joint venture.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-run Korea Heavy Industries and Construction Corp said on Wednesday it had agreed with China's Jiang Nam Shipyard to set up a joint venture in Shanghai, China, to make ship engines.</p>
<p>The two companies and several others, including Man B&amp;W Diesel AS of Denmark, will initially invest a total of $20 million in the joint venture, a Korea Heavy statement said.</p>
<p>The statement said annual sales of the joint venture were expected to reach about $160 million when the plant starts operations in 1999.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5646</p>
</text>
